-- title:
--   Truncated norm-p idele lies in the prime Hecke set
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and a prime $p$, and assume [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b p`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87): $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $u$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_u$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $p\in u$. Let $O$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an Eichler order of level $M$, i.e. $O=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two orders maximal under inclusion among orders, with $[\Lambda_1:O]=M$, and assume $p\nmid M$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq p$ and let $v$ be a height-one prime containing $q$. Let $w\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ have reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(w)=w_{\mathrm{re}}^2-aw_I^2-bw_J^2+ab\,w_K^2=p$, and suppose that for every height-one prime $u\neq v$ not containing $p$ the image of $w$ in $(\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_u)^{\times}$ lies in [`Submodule.localBoxUnits O u`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45), i.e. it and its inverse lie in the additive group generated by the $z\otimes c$ with $z\in O$ and $c$ a $u$-adic integer. Let $t$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose $u$-component is $w\otimes 1$ for every $u$ not containing $q$ and $1$ for every $u$ containing $q$. Then $t\in$ [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet O p`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109): both $t$ and $p\cdot t^{-1}$ lie in the adelic box of $O$, while neither $t^{-1}$ nor $p^{-1}\cdot t$ does.
--
--   This identifies the idele obtained from a global quaternion of reduced norm $p$ by truncating it to $1$ above $q$ as an element of the Hecke set at the ramified prime $p$, so that it represents the Hecke operator $T_p$ (a shift by a local uniformiser) on the class set of the Eichler order. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.classSet_mk_eq_classSetShift_mk_of_finiteAdeleEvalAt_eq_mul_of_nrd_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.classSet_mk_eq_classSetShift_mk_of_finiteAdeleEvalAt_eq_mul_of_nrd_eq) to compare classes in the quaternionic class set with their shifts.
